 # SkillStreaks
-SkillStreaks OSRS plugin+
+SkillStreaks is a RuneLite external plugin that tracks consecutive XP gains in the same OSRS skill. When the same skill gains XP repeatedly, the plugin keeps a running streak count, records the best streak for the session, and can announce streak milestones in the in-game chat box.
+
+## Features
+
+- Tracks `StatChanged` XP events from the RuneLite client.
+- Continues the streak when the next XP gain is in the same skill and has higher XP than the previous event.
+- Resets the current streak when XP switches to another skill.
+- Keeps a best-streak value for the current RuneLite session.
+- Ignores the `Overall` pseudo-skill by default so duplicate aggregate XP events do not inflate streaks.
+- Uses only local RuneLite client events; no external API calls or network credentials are required.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Open RuneLite's plugin configuration panel and search for `SkillStreaks`.
+
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Announce streaks | On | Sends a game chat message when a skill streak reaches the configured threshold. |
+| Minimum streak | 3 | Minimum consecutive XP gains in the same skill before announcements appear. |
+| Track overall XP | Off | Includes the `Overall` pseudo-skill in tracking. Usually leave this off. |
+
+## Development
+
+This repository follows the standard RuneLite external plugin layout:
+
+- `src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/skillstreaks/SkillStreaksPlugin.java` - plugin entry point and streak logic.
+- `src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/skillstreaks/SkillStreaksConfig.java` - RuneLite configuration items.
+- `src/test/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/skillstreaks/SkillStreaksPluginTest.java` - lightweight unit tests plus the local RuneLite launcher used by the Gradle `run` task.
+- `runelite-plugin.properties` - Plugin Hub metadata used by RuneLite's external plugin loader.
+
+Use Java 11 when building locally:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+./gradlew test --no-daemon -q
+./gradlew assemble --no-daemon -q
+```
+
+To launch RuneLite in developer mode with this plugin loaded:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+./gradlew run --no-daemon
+```
+
+## Manual testing checklist
+
+Before plugin-hub prep or release, manually verify in RuneLite developer mode:
+
+1. Enable `SkillStreaks` in the plugin panel.
+2. Leave `Track overall XP` disabled and gain XP in one skill at least three times; confirm a chat message appears at the configured threshold.
+3. Gain XP in a different skill; confirm the current streak resets to `x1` and the previous best streak is preserved.
+4. Change `Minimum streak` and confirm announcements respect the new threshold.
+5. Toggle `Announce streaks` off and confirm tracking continues silently with no chat spam.
+6. Optionally enable `Track overall XP` and confirm overall XP events are included only when that setting is on.
+
+## Plugin Hub notes
+
+The plugin is self-contained and does not call WiseOldMan, TempleOSRS, or any other external API. Plugin Hub prep should focus on manual RuneLite behavior verification, a screenshot/GIF of the chat announcement, final icon review, and the normal `runelite-plugin.properties` metadata review.
